{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/952357-plant-spirits-as-a-familiar","id":952357,"title":"Plant spirits as a familiar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-16T23:50:43-07:00","id":952357,"title":"Plant spirits as a familiar","content":"I posted this in the Mage forum, but I haven't received any responses yet so I figured I'd try here. I'm playing in a mixed campaign, including werewolves. We use bits and pieces of the cosmology from all of the games, but when dealing with the Umbra we default to Werewolf. This is why I posted here, because I'm guessing the regulars here would have some helpful information. My character is a mage with a decent amount of Spirit and Life. He has recently covered a very large building in ivy, intending on awakening the spirit of the ivy and using it as a sentient defense system. The storyteller half-jokingly mentioned using the ivy spirit as a familiar, and I actually thought that might be a cool idea. The problem is I don't know too much about the types of spirits in Werewolf so I don't really know how plant spirits act and whether or not they'd be useful familiars. So I was hoping someone with more familiarity could tell me what plants spirits are like in W:tA or tell me what book to look in to find examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T09:21:39-07:00","id":952560,"title":"","content":"Check out Axis Mundi (I prefer the older edition), it has some examples of plant spirits. Generally I portray plant spirits not so different from other spirits associated with terrain- they are not as gregarious as animal spirits and what they care about is usually more staid and predictable. I like the idea of an ivy spirit creeping and slinking along, maybe even getting a little handsy without realizing it.<br /> <br /> As for whether it is 'useful' or not, that is up to you. There is the standard 'tangles up your enemies' route, but it could have other charms and abilities depending on what you want it to do. Using tumble-down stone and jagged shards of mortar as bludgeoning weapons might be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:10:17-07:00","id":952626,"title":"","content":"The plant spirits of Axis Mundo make better totems than familiars (I especially like using Corn Maiden as a Totem for Sorcerers because of the gifts that her followers can take).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:19:24-07:00","id":952660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/952357-plant-spirits-as-a-familiar?p=952560#post952560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out Axis Mundi (I prefer the older edition), it has some examples of plant spirits. Generally I portray plant spirits not so different from other spirits associated with terrain- they are not as gregarious as animal spirits and what they care about is usually more staid and predictable. I like the idea of an ivy spirit creeping and slinking along, maybe even getting a little handsy without realizing it.<br /> <br /> As for whether it is 'useful' or not, that is up to you. There is the standard 'tangles up your enemies' route, but it could have other charms and abilities depending on what you want it to do. Using tumble-down stone and jagged shards of mortar as bludgeoning weapons might be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. Chapter 4 of Axis Mundi has a bit on plant spirits.<br /> <br /> The Changeling Players Guide also had a section Nunnehi which might be of help.<br /> For Mage, Spirit Ways is good for that sort of thing. There is a chapter on Spirit Helpers but I don't remember what specifically it covers.<br /> <br /> When it comes down to it, I would guess that you are mostly just going to be building the familiar with the Mage familiar background system and that anything else is purely fluff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/952357-plant-spirits-as-a-familiar?p=952626#post952626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The plant spirits of Axis Mundo make better totems than familiars (I especially like using Corn Maiden as a Totem for Sorcerers because of the gifts that her followers can take).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that for the +3 to all social rolls involving Humans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 08-17-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:57:06-07:00","id":952687,"title":"","content":"That, and access to Gifts of dealing with food, natural cycles, and weather (since you do not need to be Kinfolk or Garou to learn them from your Totem if you are a Sorcerer, and you are only limited by you negotiations with your Totem on the level and types of Gifts you can access).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:15:51-07:00","id":952704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/952357-plant-spirits-as-a-familiar?p=952687#post952687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">since you do not need to be Kinfolk or Garou to learn them from your Totem if you are a Sorcerer, and you are only limited by you negotiations with your Totem on the level and types of Gifts you can access.</div> </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as incredibly odd. Do you have a page reference for Sorcerers learning gifts? Especially Gifts of higher rank?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:41:00-07:00","id":952717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/952357-plant-spirits-as-a-familiar?p=952704#post952704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This strikes me as incredibly odd. Do you have a page reference for Sorcerers learning gifts? Especially Gifts of higher rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes this seems very incorrect. Garou can learn gifts purely because of the Pact, which is made possible because they are half spirit. Kinfolk can learn them as a side effect of garou blood.<br /> <br /> You seem to be saying anyone can learn gifts, which is pretty much saying anyone can just make a new The Pact, which is right up there a feat as Caine Cursing the Clans with Generation and unique curses in one night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T14:46:21-07:00","id":952750,"title":"","content":"Sorcerer: The Hedge Wizard's Handbook, p. 70.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:58:30-07:00","id":952804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/952357-plant-spirits-as-a-familiar?p=952750#post952750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerer: The Hedge Wizard's Handbook, p. 70.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an early edition book, with all of the silliness that comes with that. The same Merit was reprinted in Sorcerer Revised with the part about the Gift learning removed. There is a reason for that. In any case, even if you did allow a Sorcerer to learn Gifts, I don't see how you could interpret that to mean that they can learn <i>any</i> rank Gifts. They have no method of gaining rank.<br /> <br /> You can obviously (and will) run it however you want, but interpreting the books that way, and cherry picking which edition's wording to use, strikes me as incorrect.<br /> <br /> On the Corn Maiden Totem specifically, I would also argue those Traits and Ban are specifically tailored for Garou. A human follower would have different Traits (there are examples the same Totem giving different traits to different creatures). Giving +3 dice to <u>all</u> social rolls (since 99% of the time Sorcerers are interacting with people) comes off as pure min/maxing.<br /> Maize (Corn) appears as a Totem for the Nunnehi, and the stats there are much more fitting for a Sorcerer to use (Empathy 2, Cooking 2, +1 Wits). Similar-ish Ban. I don't see you being open to the suggestion though, since you would prefer to use the one that increases every social roll ever for a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T16:38:38-07:00","id":952836,"title":"","content":"speaking of this crossover issue?<br /> <br /> What happens when Hedge Magicians, Mages or (Gaia Forbid) Tremere Vampires, summon up vampires, <br /> <br /> and they file a complaint, been thinking of bringing that up... but a way to explain to myself why doing so wasnt just abandoned all together aeons ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}